          %title Uniformly regular spaces
          %h1#uniformly_regular_spaces Uniformly regular spaces
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#compact_spaces"} Compact spaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#regularity"} Regularity
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#apartness"} Apartness
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#locatedness"} Locatedness
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#uniform_apartness_spaces"} Uniform apartness spaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_pages"} Related pages
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+regular+space"} completely regular space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %em uniformly regular
            uniform space is an intermediate notion in between regularity and complete regularity for uniform spaces, which is frequently useful in the constructive theory of uniform spaces; classically every uniform space is uniformly regular. (Indeed, some authors include uniform regularity in the constructive
            %em definition
            of a uniform space.)
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is defined in terms of entourages, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong uniformly regular
            if it satisfies the following property:
          %ul
            %li
              For every entourage
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi V
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg{V} \cup U = X \times X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg{V}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo ≈
                        %mi U
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∨
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ≉
                        %mi V
                      %mi y
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall U,\; \exists V,\; \forall x, y,\; x \approx_U y \;\vee\; x \mathbin{&amp;#8777;}_V y .
          %p
            With
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            itself, so every uniform structure is uniformly regular in classical mathematics. Note that any uniformity induced by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+space"} gauge
            is uniformly regular (as long as the gauging distances take values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+real+numbers"} located real numbers
            as is usually understood).
          %p
            When the uniformity of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is defined in terms of uniform covers, then the equivalent condition is:
          %ul
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a uniform cover, there exists a uniform cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              such that, for any two points
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in A
              for some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in B
              for no
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in C'
          %p
            With
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Note that uniform regularity is not literally a “uniformization” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regularity
            but rather of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+decomposable+space"} local decomposability
            = succeed "." do
              %strong uniform local decomposability
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-uniform+spaces"} quasi-uniform spaces
            (and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+convergence+spaces"} uniform convergence spaces
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+space"} gauge space
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+real+numbers"} located real numbers
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ε
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi ε
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{d,\varepsilon} = \{ (x,y) \mid d(x,y)\lt\varepsilon \}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
