                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt \varepsilon/2
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete
                uniform space is uniformly regular if and only if the underlying set has
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+equality"} decidable equality
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular
                if and only if it has decidable equality.) Thus, the statement “every uniform space is (uniformly) regular” is equivalent to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %li
              %p
                In particular, not every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
                is uniformly regular: any group without decidable equality can be equipped with the discrete topology. However, the classical examples of Lie groups and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
                (TVSs) are uniformly regular.
            %li
              %p
                However, if a topological group is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is any neighborhood of the identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                in a topological group
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
